.TH jirakeep 1 "" "jirakeep 0.1.0" "General Commands Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
jirakeep \- MCP server for Atlassian Jira Cloud with operator\-controlled security guards
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBjirakeep\fR
\fB\-\-jira\-server\fR <JIRA_SERVER>
[\fB\-\-transport\fR <TRANSPORT>]
[\fB\-\-host\fR <HOST>]
[\fB\-\-port\fR <PORT>]
[\fB\-\-api\-key\-header\fR <API_KEY_HEADER>]
[\fB\-\-email\-header\fR <EMAIL_HEADER>]
[\fB\-\-api\-key\fR <API_KEY>]
[\fB\-\-api\-key\-file\fR <API_KEY_FILE>]
[\fB\-\-email\fR <EMAIL>]
[\fB\-\-email\-file\fR <EMAIL_FILE>]
[\fB\-\-read\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-policy\fR <POLICY>]
[\fB\-\-audit\-config\fR <AUDIT_CONFIG>]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
MCP server for Atlassian Jira Cloud with operator\-controlled security guards
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-jira\-server\fR \fI<JIRA_SERVER>\fR
Base URL of the Jira Cloud site (e.g. \*(Aqhttps://example.atlassian.net\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<TRANSPORT>\fR [default: http]
Transport for the MCP server: \*(Aqhttp\*(Aq (default) or \*(Aqstdio\*(Aq
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
http: Streamable HTTP transport (default)
.IP \(bu 2
stdio: Stdio transport
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fI<HOST>\fR [default: 127.0.0.1]
Host address for the MCP server to listen on (http transport only)
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR [default: 8000]
Port for the MCP server to listen on (http transport only)
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\-header\fR \fI<API_KEY_HEADER>\fR [default: ApiKey]
HTTP header for clients to send the Jira API token
.TP
\fB\-\-email\-header\fR \fI<EMAIL_HEADER>\fR [default: X\-Atlassian\-Email]
HTTP header for clients to send the Atlassian account email (per\-request Cloud Basic auth when \-\-email is not set on the server)
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR \fI<API_KEY>\fR
Jira Cloud API token
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\-file\fR \fI<API_KEY_FILE>\fR
Path to a file holding the Jira Cloud API token
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Atlassian account email for Cloud Basic auth
.TP
\fB\-\-email\-file\fR \fI<EMAIL_FILE>\fR
Path to a file holding the Atlassian account email
.TP
\fB\-\-read\-only\fR
Disables all tools which modify Jira state
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fI<POLICY>\fR
Path to the guard policy TOML file
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\-config\fR \fI<AUDIT_CONFIG>\fR
Path to the audit configuration TOML file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Startup or runtime failure: an unreadable policy, a key/email
misconfiguration, a Jira client or transport error.
.TP
.B 2
Command\-line usage error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each variable is the fallback for one option; a command\-line argument
always wins over the environment, and the built\-in default applies when
neither is given.
.TP
.B JIRA_SERVER
Fallback for \fB\-\-jira\-server\fR.
.TP
.B MCP_TRANSPORT
Fallback for \fB\-\-transport\fR.
.TP
.B MCP_HOST
Fallback for \fB\-\-host\fR.
.TP
.B MCP_PORT
Fallback for \fB\-\-port\fR.
.TP
.B MCP_API_KEY_HEADER
Fallback for \fB\-\-api\-key\-header\fR.
.TP
.B MCP_EMAIL_HEADER
Fallback for \fB\-\-email\-header\fR.
.TP
.B JIRA_API_TOKEN
Fallback for \fB\-\-api\-key\fR.
.TP
.B JIRA_API_TOKEN_FILE
Fallback for \fB\-\-api\-key\-file\fR.
.TP
.B JIRA_EMAIL
Fallback for \fB\-\-email\fR.
.TP
.B JIRA_EMAIL_FILE
Fallback for \fB\-\-email\-file\fR.
.TP
.B MCP_READ_ONLY
Fallback for \fB\-\-read\-only\fR.
.TP
.B JIRAKEEP_POLICY
Fallback for \fB\-\-policy\fR.
.TP
.B JIRAKEEP_AUDIT_CONFIG
Fallback for \fB\-\-audit\-config\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/jirakeep/policy.toml
Worked example guard policy as installed by distribution packages; the
source tree and release archives ship it as
.IR examples/policy.toml .
The server reads a policy only when one is named with
.B \-\-policy
or
.BR JIRAKEEP_POLICY ;
without one the built\-in allow\-all default policy applies.
.SH EXAMPLES
Serve a local MCP client over stdio:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
jirakeep \-\-transport stdio \e
    \-\-jira\-server https://example.atlassian.net \e
    \-\-email user@example.com \e
    \-\-api\-key\-file ~/.config/jirakeep/api\-token \e
    \-\-policy /etc/jirakeep/policy.toml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Listen on HTTP (default, 127.0.0.1:8000), each client presenting its own
token in the API key header (email still required once issue tools call
Jira with Basic auth — use server\-held mode for a full credential pair):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
jirakeep \-\-jira\-server https://example.atlassian.net \e
    \-\-policy /etc/jirakeep/policy.toml
.fi
.RE
